                        "entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "и́зы́сках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                        "entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "нечто необычное, изысканное, красивое; утончённость, новшество в чём-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ee25a67-b50d-4320-a9be-85355c496a23",
                                "sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                                "text": "От всей души поздравляем вас и признаемся, что немного завидуем вашим домочадцам, которых вы балуете такими кулинарными изысками."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b04c729a-7d4c-4735-ab96-b3bc8f8eab08",
                        "source_entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "source_sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                        "target_lang_word": "extravagance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "extravagance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66b6180c-7438-357d-8ef0-e14b003c1c4b",
                                        "entry_id": "73ba55aa-e5c6-3a44-ab73-44778ec9de68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive or superfluous expenditure of money."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eeb9725c-5485-3434-bbbb-7805ee22970d",
                                        "entry_id": "73ba55aa-e5c6-3a44-ab73-44778ec9de68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prodigality, as of anger, love, expression, imagination, or demands."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5056dfc9-91b6-4998-83e7-6592ac44d674",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb9725c-5485-3434-bbbb-7805ee22970d",
                                                "text": "The visions of romance were over. Catherine was completely awakened. Henry’s address, short as it had been, had more thoroughly opened her eyes to the extravagance of her late fancies than all their several disappointments had done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e099f61e-fcbd-453c-b3ef-d95820a56bba",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb9725c-5485-3434-bbbb-7805ee22970d",
                                                "text": "A great bargain also had been the excellent Axminster carpet which covered the floor; as, again, the arm-chair in which Bunting now sat forward, staring into the dull, small fire. In fact, that arm-chair had been an extravagance of Mrs. Bunting. She had wanted her husband to be comfortable after the day's work was done, and she had paid thirty-seven shillings for the chair."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afbb4dbe-44e0-425b-b091-8194940c17ac",
                                                "sense_id": "eeb9725c-5485-3434-bbbb-7805ee22970d",
                                                "text": "At the same time he will need most carefully to avoid anything resembling extravagance or overstatement. While no socialist heorist has ever been known to discredit himself with his fellows even by the silliest of proposals, the old-fashioned liberal will damn himself by an impracticable suggestion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43f119d7-ef0f-3144-b895-bf31bbbaedae",
                                        "entry_id": "73ba55aa-e5c6-3a44-ab73-44778ec9de68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something extravagant; something done out of extravagance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0b272a4-3b47-4e9d-bed5-09ba69eb0765",
                                                "sense_id": "43f119d7-ef0f-3144-b895-bf31bbbaedae",
                                                "text": "That luxury car is an extravagance you can't afford."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24120f39-2eab-4e66-8d1b-38a6bc366309",
                                                "sense_id": "43f119d7-ef0f-3144-b895-bf31bbbaedae",
                                                "text": "There were no limos or extravagances at this point, because we all wanted to make as much money as possible. We played it cheap. No huge catering bills, no wild parties, not even upgraded hotel rooms. Whenever we arrived at an airport Robin would be there to meet us in a rented SUV or big sedan, and we'd head to the gig on our own."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1c640d56-3d4f-4a7d-bd5f-0f7ce9582e6f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "source_sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                        "target_lang_word": "outlandishness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "outlandishness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59ff1411-271b-3687-af09-7fc1e792b3a6",
                                        "entry_id": "ae45a689-e1da-32f1-8de0-7f78eb55de0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being outlandish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "732fc66c-7c75-4e32-86ad-1172aec2300a",
                                                "sense_id": "59ff1411-271b-3687-af09-7fc1e792b3a6",
                                                "text": "Mini-golf and go-cart parks had exploded, each striving to outdo its literally dozens of competitors in outlandishness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e2e20c3-8a32-4f27-b525-98cd29020f29",
                        "source_entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "source_sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                        "target_lang_word": "oddity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "oddity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An odd or strange thing or opinion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92e088b3-c714-43a6-9426-d063213a1f19",
                                                "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had then none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after days when I came in contact with the Celebrity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccab287e-8a0c-41f3-af3b-1d2f74961972",
                                                "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                                "text": "An Avonside 0-4-4T with outside cylinders, bought by the S.M.A. in 1882 and scrapped in 1892 as a dismal failure, was one of the motive power oddities (some of them mortgaged)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "891a258e-a7c5-38ab-80d4-2f0e81bd26ea",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A strange person; an oddball."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6c3ac3b-bdba-4929-b562-9445cb90f14a",
                                                "sense_id": "891a258e-a7c5-38ab-80d4-2f0e81bd26ea",
                                                "text": "Fête succeeded fête in honour of the arrival of Christina of Sweden, who seemed to communicate her own reckless love of novelty to the then somewhat staid French court. Claim your privileges as an oddity, and even you yourself will be astonished at their extent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f79b181-a7fb-35cc-82fe-fdff1cee1541",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Strangeness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba090a78-d583-40a7-a6b6-b16c69b42be2",
                                                "sense_id": "4f79b181-a7fb-35cc-82fe-fdff1cee1541",
                                                "text": "The thing was unprecedented in his experience, and probably he wondered in his equine way at the eccentricities of the human race, and questioned whether oddity might not be merging into insanity in his master’s case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "418f7eff-85b1-4374-9f18-fb25837989fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
                        "source_sense_id": "df615937-a11a-35bd-9ed4-52742e3c961a",
                        "target_lang_word": "pretentiousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pretentiousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                        "entry_id": "554481e6-6ed2-3002-9df1-a305e625f734",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being pretentious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbf8f209-047e-4d84-9737-6f765068849d",
                                                "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: affectation, affectedness, false pretense, pretending"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f20a907c-e3f4-4303-9f6e-071efd9e446e",
                                                "sense_id": "460f4571-21d6-3c5a-8edc-6fde37595ba4",
                                                "text": "Possibly her sheer pretentiousness, or that she knew everything about everything, or maybe because she treated her reporters like underoxygenated platypies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "44c18b4e-ef96-4f40-b603-45489c84909f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b09983cf-456f-343e-8611-6c9b61d59fa4",
